# Spec test coverage

A child spec is not done until tests cover **at least 70%** of **that spec’s new behavior** (aim **80%**). Count Done-when / behaviour bullets of the new work — not whole-repo line coverage.

- Web: Vitest, colocated `*.test.ts` next to the helpers (see `lib/progress/helpers.test.ts`).
- Go: `go test` beside the package.
- Do not tick Done or mark 000 / README **done** without a tests checkbox that passed.
- Skip only what cannot be automated: Netlify UI clicks, MapLibre tiles, generated files, story copy.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — spec lands parse/migrate with no tests
export const parseSnapshot = (raw: string | null): Snapshot => { /* ... */ };

// ✅ GOOD — same helpers, cases for the new behaviour
describe("parseSnapshot", () => {
  it("unwraps a zustand persist blob", () => { /* ... */ });
  it("accepts a flat snapshot", () => { /* ... */ });
});
```
